# Environment Configuration Template

## Server Configuration
# .env for server application

# Application Settings
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=5000
APP_URL=http://localhost:5000

# Database Configuration
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://mongodb:27017/pastebox
DB_NAME=pastebox

# Authentication
JWT_SECRET=your_jwt_secret_key_here_make_it_long_and_random
JWT_EXPIRE=7d

# AWS S3 Configuration
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your_aws_access_key
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your_aws_secret_key
S3_BUCKET_NAME=pastebox-files

# Email Configuration (Optional)
MAIL_USER=your_email@gmail.com
MAIL_PASS=your_app_password
MAIL_SERVICE=gmail
MAIL_FROM=noreply@pastebox.com

# File Upload Settings
MAX_FILE_SIZE=104857600  # 100MB in bytes
UPLOAD_TIMEOUT=300000    # 5 minutes in milliseconds
TEMP_DIR=/tmp/uploads

# File Expiration
DEFAULT_EXPIRY_DAYS=7
MAX_EXPIRY_DAYS=30

# CORS Configuration
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:5173
CORS_CREDENTIALS=true

# Logging
LOG_LEVEL=info
LOG_FORMAT=combined

---

## Client Configuration
# .env for client application

# React/Vite Settings
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000
VITE_APP_NAME=PasteBox

# API Endpoints
VITE_AUTH_ENDPOINT=/api/auth
VITE_FILES_ENDPOINT=/api/files
VITE_USERS_ENDPOINT=/api/users

# Feature Flags
VITE_ENABLE_SOCIAL_SHARE=true
VITE_ENABLE_QR_CODE=true
VITE_ENABLE_GUEST_UPLOAD=true

# Analytics (Optional)
VITE_ANALYTICS_ID=
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=

---

## Testing Configuration
# Environment variables for tests

# Application URL
APP_URL=http://localhost:5173
SELENIUM_TIMEOUT=10000

# Test Database (Optional)
TEST_MONGODB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/pastebox-test

# Test Credentials
TEST_USER_EMAIL=testuser@example.com
TEST_USER_PASSWORD=TestPassword123

# Browser Configuration
BROWSER=chrome
HEADLESS=false
WINDOW_WIDTH=1920
WINDOW_HEIGHT=1080

---

## Docker Configuration
# Environment variables for Docker Compose

# MongoDB
MONGO_INITDB_ROOT_USERNAME=admin
MONGO_INITDB_ROOT_PASSWORD=password
MONGO_INITDB_DATABASE=pastebox

# Network
NETWORK_NAME=pastebox-network

# Services
SERVER_PORT=5000
CLIENT_PORT=80
MONGODB_PORT=27017

---

## CI/CD Configuration
# Jenkins/Pipeline Environment

# Build Settings
BUILD_NUMBER=1
BUILD_TIMEOUT=3600

# Docker Registry
DOCKER_REGISTRY=your-registry
DOCKER_USERNAME=your-username
DOCKER_PASSWORD=your-password

# Deployment
DEPLOYMENT_ENV=staging
DEPLOYMENT_DOMAIN=staging.pastebox.com

---

## Production Secrets (Store in Jenkins/SecureStore)

These should NEVER be committed to git:
- JWT_SECRET
- AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID
- AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
- MAIL_PASS
- MONGO_INITDB_ROOT_PASSWORD
- DOCKER_PASSWORD

Store them in Jenkins Credentials Store:
1. Jenkins Dashboard → Manage Jenkins → Credentials
2. Store → Jenkins → Global Credentials
3. Add credentials with appropriate scope

---

## Local Development Setup

```bash
# Copy template to actual env file
cp .env.example .env
cp server/.env.example server/.env
cp client/.env.example client/.env

# Edit files with your configuration
vim server/.env
vim client/.env

# Start with docker-compose
docker-compose up -d

# Or run locally
cd server && npm start  # Terminal 1
cd client && npm run dev # Terminal 2
```

## Production Deployment

For production:
1. Use strong random values for secrets
2. Store secrets in secure credential manager
3. Use HTTPS URLs
4. Set NODE_ENV=production
5. Enable logging
6. Configure backups
7. Set up monitoring

